;; @also-unfused
;; #1429 asks whether fold, and at with a constant index, read the whole
;; column or the rows a where: keeps, under by: and keyless.  Until the
;; owner decides, #1401's keyless change leaves every such answer as it was
;; before it.  These are its parent's (ec0630a0) answers, every one, keyless
;; and under by:, with and without where:, alone and beside a declined
;; output: a constant index written in place, fold, and under a where: an
;; index computed from no column.  Without a where: a computed index reads
;; every row either way, (sum (at c (til 4))) is #1402's and keyless_agg_
;; source_whole pins it.  med is left out: under by: its answer over such a
;; source reads memory it did not write and differs run to run, on the
;; parent too (#1572).
